  {
    "id": 1002,
    "type": "post",
    "slug": "multiple-imputation-chained-equations",
    "path": "/posts/multiple-imputation-chained-equations",
    "url": "https://castellanos.biostatistician.page/posts/multiple-imputation-chained-equations",
    "title": "Notes on multiple imputation with chained equations",
    "excerpt": "A working checklist for MICE in R, with the defaults I change and why.",
    "content": {
      "html": "<p>These notes collect what I tell students before they run <code>mice()</code> on a real data set.</p><h2>Set up the predictor matrix first</h2><p>The default uses every variable to impute every other variable. That is rarely what you want when the data include IDs or derived scores.</p><pre><code class=\"language-r\">library(mice)\nimp &lt;- mice(dat, m = 20, maxit = 0)\npred &lt;- imp$predictorMatrix\npred[, \"patient_id\"] &lt;- 0\nfit &lt;- with(mice(dat, m = 20, predictorMatrix = pred), lm(sbp ~ age + bmi))\npool(fit)</code></pre><h3>Check convergence</h3><p>Plot the chains with <code>plot(imp)</code>. If the means drift after iteration 10, raise <code>maxit</code> and look for variables that predict each other almost perfectly.</p>",
      "json": {
        "type": "doc",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "These notes collect what I tell students before they run "
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "mice()",
                "marks": [
                  {
                    "type": "code"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": " on a real data set."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "heading",
            "attrs": {
              "level": 2
            },
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Set up the predictor matrix first"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "The default uses every variable to impute every other variable. That is rarely what you want when the data include IDs or derived scores."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "codeBlock",
            "attrs": {
              "language": "r"
            },
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "library(mice)\nimp <- mice(dat, m = 20, maxit = 0)\npred <- imp$predictorMatrix\npred[, \"patient_id\"] <- 0\nfit <- with(mice(dat, m = 20, predictorMatrix = pred), lm(sbp ~ age + bmi))\npool(fit)"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "heading",
            "attrs": {
              "level": 3
            },
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Check convergence"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Plot the chains with "
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "plot(imp)",
                "marks": [
                  {
                    "type": "code"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ". If the means drift after iteration 10, raise "
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "maxit",
                "marks": [
                  {
                    "type": "code"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": " and look for variables that predict each other almost perfectly."
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    },
