  {
    "id": 1004,
    "type": "post",
    "slug": "reviewing-forty-survival-analyses",
    "path": "/posts/reviewing-forty-survival-analyses",
    "url": "https://castellanos.biostatistician.page/posts/reviewing-forty-survival-analyses",
    "title": "What I learned reviewing 40 survival analyses",
    "excerpt": "Most problems came from the time axis, not the model.",
    "content": {
      "html": "<p>Last year I reviewed forty manuscripts that used Cox models. The <strong><em>same three problems</em></strong> came up again and again.</p><figure><img src=\"{{ASSETS}}/9103/conversions/km-curves-large.svg\" alt=\"Two Kaplan-Meier survival curves that cross at month 18\" data-media-id=\"103\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Crossing curves are a reason to look past the hazard ratio.</figcaption></figure><ol><li><p>Time zero did not match eligibility.</p></li><li><p>Hazard ratios were reported for crossing curves.</p></li><li><p>Competing risks were treated as censoring.</p></li></ol><p>The fix for the first one is cheap.<br>The fix for the third one is not, and it changes the estimand. <s>Reporting a sensitivity analysis is enough.</s> A sensitivity analysis does not fix the estimand.</p>",
      "json": {
        "type": "doc",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Last year I reviewed forty manuscripts that used Cox models. The "
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "same three problems",
                "marks": [
                  {
                    "type": "bold"
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "italic"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": " came up again and again."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "image",
            "attrs": {
              "src": "{{ASSETS}}/9103/conversions/km-curves-large.svg",
              "alt": "Two Kaplan-Meier survival curves that cross at month 18",
              "title": null,
              "data-media-id": "103"
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "orderedList",
            "attrs": {
              "start": 1
            },
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "listItem",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "text",
                        "text": "Time zero did not match eligibility."
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "listItem",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "text",
                        "text": "Hazard ratios were reported for crossing curves."
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "listItem",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "text",
                        "text": "Competing risks were treated as censoring."
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "The fix for the first one is cheap."
              },
              {
                "type": "hardBreak"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "The fix for the third one is not, and it changes the estimand. "
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Reporting a sensitivity analysis is enough.",
                "marks": [
                  {
                    "type": "strike"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": " A sensitivity analysis does not fix the estimand."
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    "author": {
      "name": "Imani Castellanos"
